ing: with LeaderLeaseTimeout of one second the partitioned leader returned twenty \\\"\n         \\\"successful verifications over about 1,015 ms before stepping down, so the window tracks the configured lease but was not varied.\\\")\nassert old_lim in new['limitations']\nnew['limitations']=[new_lim if l==old_lim else l for l in new['limitations']]\nnew['joint_history']=(\\\"Receipt e49121154f514e39b6c1a37a2c353a4a is the successor of 533b966489544f45b4fcf14f6edce57f-experiment under this \\\"\n  \\\"question: identical cases, admissions and first-verification assertions, with an added repeat loop. The two receipts agree on the decisive \\\"\n  \\\"outcomes (trigger succeeds, control fails), so they describe the same subject; the successor adds the exposure measurement the earlier \\\"\n  \\\"receipt lacked.\\\")\njson.dump({'rationale':(\\\"Add the successor receipt to the VerifyLeader account: repeated verification succeeded twenty times across about 1,015 ms \\\"\n  \\\"before the lease stepped the partitioned leader down, against zero successes in the control. The previously unmeasured exposure-window \\\"\n  \\\"limitation is replaced by the measured window at one lease setting, and both receipts are cited with joint history.\\\"),\n 'interpretations':[new]},open('draft/update.json','w'),indent=2)\nprint('ce',len(new['counterevidence']),'lim',len(new['limitations']))\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
